    "protocol_name": "EtherCAT",
    "version": "ETG.1000",
    "description": "EtherCAT frames (EtherType 0x88A4) of datagrams sent by the master and returned by the slaves; the first datagram command selects the message type. Datagram data is the addressed slave memory / process image and is one bytes field. Derived from the Wireshark/tshark dissection of the benchmark capture (dol/truth-file-derivation/scripts/build_truth.py): fields at a fixed offset in at least 60% of a type's messages, bitfields sharing a byte merged, arrays of 3+ equal fields and variable-position content kept as one bytes field (the modbus.json convention for register arrays); types with fewer than 5 messages are omitted.",
    "offset_convention": "The 2-byte frame header uses wire-absolute offsets; datagram types are relative to the first datagram (offset 0 = command = wire offset 2).",
